/ AFL+ASan corpus sweep 2026-07-14 (round 5): bugs found by running the
/ minimized AFL corpus (corpus_min2, ~30k coverage-unique inputs) through an
/ ASan+UBSan build -- crashes/UB that plain AFL (which only sees SIGSEGV/hang)
/ sailed past.  Error-path cases use the @[f;x;:] trap so a value prints.

/ 1. sv/vs base conversion: the i64 Horner accumulator and mixed-radix place
/    products overflowed signed i64 on an over-wide value -- UB (ubsan trap).
/    Now computed in u64: the same defined-wrap result, no UB.
2 sv 2 -9223372036854775808j 4
24 60 60 sv 1 2 3
2 sv 1 0 1 0 1
2 sv 2 vs 100
1 2 3~2 60 60 vs 3723

/ 2. sv with an EMPTY base vector: `*\|a` was empty, so a count decrement
/    underflowed to SIZE_MAX and the next reverse tried a ~2^64-byte alloc
/    (silent death in production).  No places => decode is 0.
(^10) sv 3
(!0) sv 100

/ 3. do-n scan `n f\x` with n = 0Ij (INT64_MAX): the result list was sized
/    1+n, which overflowed to a negative count -> ~2^64 alloc -> SEGFAULT in
/    production.  Now a clean `limit` error.
@[{0Ij{x+1}\x};0;:]
@[{9223372036854775807j{x}\x};0;:]

/ 4. dyadic `$` (format) with a non-finite / out-of-i64-range width fed the
/    float straight into a float->i64 cast -- UB.  inf/huge now `wsfull`
/    (as production already returned via its post-cast check), nan `value`.
@[{0ie$3.5};0;:]
@[{1e30e$5};0;:]
0.0e$"3.5"

